      "content": "Wait, it's actually talking about \"satisfying the algorithm\" in the description itself? I mean, I guess that works, but the description should be for the app users, not for the code lol. \n\nStill, the richness score is improving, but I'm worried it's getting a bit wordy. Let's try a different piece to see if we can get a truly massive score. \n\nThis one is a glass sculpture: It's a small, clear sphere of hand-blown glass sitting on a wooden base. It's very smooth and reflects a lot of light. \n\nTry to get the score as high as humanly possible for this one. Don't worry about making it a long paragraph, just make sure the ratio of adjectives to words is insanely high so the algorithm picks it up immediately.",
